Package: linop.primme
Title: The 'PRIMME' Eigensolver as a Compiled Engine for 'linop'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Gilles", "Colling", email = "gilles.colling051@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3070-6066")),
    person("Andreas", "Stathopoulos", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "PRIMME library"),
    person("Eloy", "Romero", role = c("ctb", "cph"), comment = "PRIMME library"),
    person("Lingfei", "Wu", role = c("ctb", "cph"), comment = "PRIMME library"),
    person("College of William & Mary", role = "cph",
           comment = "PRIMME library"))
Description: Bindings to the 'PRIMME' library (Stathopoulos and McCombs 2010,
    <doi:10.1145/1731022.1731031>; Wu, Romero and Stathopoulos 2017,
    <doi:10.1137/16M1082214>) for a few eigenpairs of a Hermitian operator and a
    few singular triplets of a rectangular one, both given only by their action.
    'PRIMME' 3.2.3 is vendored and linked against R's own Basic Linear Algebra
    Subprograms ('BLAS') and 'LAPACK'. The package is the engine behind method = "primme" in the 'linop' package and
    exposes no interface of its own beyond the two calls 'linop' makes.
